<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!-- TEI.extensions.ent file for the TEI, where the TEI is to be generated	-->
<!-- by the TEI Pizza Chef at http://www.tei-c.org/pizza.html				-->
<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!-- The TEI Pizza Chef settings:											-->
<!-- Generated by selecting: - Mixed base tagset: Prose and Verse			-->
<!-- Toppings: linking, figures, analysis, transcr, textcrit, names/dates,  -->
<!-- corpora																-->
<!-- No entity set chosen as there is a complete entity set given in the 	-->
<!-- extension files.														-->
<!-- Modification files selected: norron.extensions.ent and 				-->
<!-- norron.extensions.dtd													-->
<!-- Generate full DTD pressed 												-->
<!-- ********************************************************************* 	-->
<!-- Made for the research group: 											-->
<!-- Editing medieval manuscripts 											-->
<!-- Centre for Advanced Study												-->
<!-- Norway, 2000-2004. 													-->
<!-- Further changed and updated for the Menota project, see				-->		
<!-- http://www.hit.uib.no/menota/, by Tone Merete Bruvik, Aksis,			-->
<!-- see http://www.aksis.uib.no/											-->
<!-- Norway, 2001-2004. 													-->
<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!-- When changing extension files, please observe:							-->
<!-- Has to be in SGML syntax. 												-->
<!-- Character with hex value grater than 7F is not allowed anywhere in 	-->
<!-- the extension files due to restrictions in the Pizza Chef.  			-->
<!-- Comments can not contain series of hyphens.							-->
<!-- *********************************************************************	-->

<!-- April 28-30, 2004 TMB: Added comments, elements 'orig' and 'reg' 
are not removed anylonger and changes to the elements 'tagUsage' and 'keywords'
are removed. -->

<!-- March 16, 2004 Odd Einar Haugen: Updated the list with additional 
entities for U+014B (sc. "punct") and U+00DF (sc. "ssharp"), renamed 
"thscap" to "thornscap", and added U+1D18 "pscap". -->

<!-- March 15, 2004, TMB: removed type from the class of metrical 
attributes. -->

<!-- February 6, 2004 Odd Einar Haugen: Made a complete revision of the 
list of entities so that it conforms to the MUFI character recommendation, 
version 1.0 (published December 8, 2003); cf. its persistent URL:                    http://www.ub.uib.no/elpub/2003/r/000001/                       -->

<!-- May 20, 2003 Odd Einar Haugen: Added entity &apos; in section (1) 
below.	-->

<!-- May 15, 2003 Odd Einar Haugen: Made a complete revision of the list of 
entities, which now conforms to standard ISO entities (HTML 4.0). 	
Entities outside HTML 4.0 have been defined according to the rules set 
out in the Menota handbook (presently in ch. 2.2, 5 and 6 of version 1.0). 
All entities are defined with reference to Unicode code points in 
version 3.2 of this standard, including many in the Private Use Area. 
Combining diacritical marks have been allocated separate entity names, 
which allows for equivalent encodings of many characters. For example, 
the a with an acute accent may be encoded with the standard ISO entity 
"&aacute;" or as a sequence of an "a"		and "&combacute;", the latter 
referring to COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT, 0301 in Unicode. Finally, the names 
of the characters are now Unicode conformant. Characters in the Private Use 
Area have been named in analogy with the Unicode system. -->

<!-- May 2, 2002 Tone Merete Bruvik: Added encoding from MASTER (see 
http://www.hcu.ox.ac.uk/TEI/Master/Reference/). -->

<!-- May 21, 2001 Tone Merete Bruvik: Modified and added new elements. 
Details about the changes are given in connection to declaration.		-->

<!-- May 21, 2001 Odd Einar Haugen: Added list of entities referring 
to the Unicode standard (for text in header and notes) and Private Use 
Area (for text in body). 					-->

<!-- May 30, 2001 Odd Einar Haugen: Added a few supralinear entities.		-->

<!-- *********************************************************************	-->

<!-- (I) Characters in the Unicode Standard version 4.0 -->
<!-- (1) Basic Latin -->
<!-- Characters which should be designed by entities (included in the
specifications for XML) -->
 
<!ENTITY quot "&#x0022;">		<!-- QUOTATION MARK -->
<!ENTITY amp "&#x0026;">		<!-- AMPERSAND -->
<!ENTITY apos "&#x0027;">		<!-- APOSTROPHE -->
<!ENTITY lt "&#x003C;">			<!-- LESS-THAN SIGN -->
<!ENTITY gt "&#x003E;">			<!-- GREATER-THAN SIGN -->

<!-- Characters in Basic Latin with separate entities for the encoding of Medieval texts -->

<!ENTITY ampet "&#x0026;">		<!-- LATIN ABBREVIATION SIGN AMPERSAND -->
<!ENTITY apo "&#x0027;">		<!-- LATIN ABBREVIATION SIGN APOSTROPHE -->
<!ENTITY punct "&#x002E;">		<!-- LATIN ABBREVIATION SIGN SPACING DOT -->
<!-- In MUFI character recommendation v. 1.0, this character was assigned the entity name "dot". -->
<!-- That is unfortunate, since the entity "dot" is used for U+02D9 in Spacing Modifying Letters.-->
<!ENTITY ed "&#x003B;">		<!-- LATIN ABBREVIATION SIGN ED -->

